# ── BUILD OUTPUT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# CMake + Ninja out-of-source. `build/` covers the normal case; the loose object
# and archive patterns cover an in-tree build, which CMake permits and which
# would otherwise scatter artifacts through src/.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk

# CMake's droppings if anyone ever configures in the source tree.
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log

# ── CTEST'S SCRATCH DIRECTORY ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log` is written into whatever directory ctest was
# invoked from. Running `ctest` from the repo root rather than from build/ is an
# easy slip — the README's own command does it via `--test-dir` — and the log
# carries absolute local paths. Ignored at any depth.
Testing/

# ── AGENT AND EDITOR STATE: personal, not project ───────────────────────────
#
# `.claude/` is one machine's permission allowlist and workflow settings. It
# tells a stranger nothing about Void Palabra and everything about one laptop,
# including absolute paths under the author's home directory. If a curated,
# path-free agent config is ever worth sharing it can be added deliberately with
# `git add -f`; the default is out.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── RUNTIME SIDECARS AND SCRATCH ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This library writes no files of its own during a normal build — Archive does
# file I/O, but only where a caller points it. These patterns exist so that a
# test run that leaves a stray artifact, or a scratch archive written beside the
# source while debugging, cannot be committed by an absent-minded `git add -A`.
*.log
*.lock
*.vpal
*.miga
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── CORRESPONDENCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `MESSAGE_FOR_*` files are inter-project handoffs between the sibling agents —
# an inbox, not a source of truth. What matters from one is folded into
# `okf/log.md` and the affected concept pages when it is acted on, which is
# where a reader should find it. Void Hormiga keeps none of them in its public
# tree for the same reason.
MESSAGE_FOR_*.md
